</div>
<p>By doing this, I was finally able to store the raw HTML into the database and retrieve it! Also, I found out for the edit form, all I needed to do was pre-populate the editor form after retrieving it from the database</p>
<div class="highlight js-code-highlight">
<pre class="highlight javascript"><code><span class="nb">document</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nx">getElementsByClassName</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="err">&lsquo;</span><span class="nx">ql</span><span class="o">-</span><span class="nx">editor</span><span class="err">&rsquo;</span><span class="p">)[</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">].</span><span class="nx">innerHTML</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="nx">topic</span><span class="p">.</span><span class="nx">content</span>
</code></pre>
<div class="highlight__panel js-actions-panel">
<div class="highlight__panel-action js-fullscreen-code-action">&nbsp;</div>
</div>
</div>
